# Updating translations

## gettext (`.po`) — never machine-translate

These rules exist because agents keep reaching for Google/`trans`/batch MT
on catalogs and then shipping msgid copies or half-broken msgstrs.

- **Forbidden for `.po` / `.pot`:** Google Translate, `trans`,
  `googletranslator`, or any other MT pipeline. Gettext is short UI strings;
  translate them yourself (or with **`poedit`** as below).
- **msgid-copy is not a translation** (exception: `msgid ""`). Empty `msgstr`
  or `msgstr == msgid` counts as untranslated.
- **≤20% completion** ⇒ treat the catalog as missing. Rewrite the whole `.po`
  by hand. Do **not** write patch/sed/Python scripts to “fix” a mostly-empty
  catalog.
- **Incremental updates** (a few new msgids): translate them yourself, then
  batch-apply with **`poedit`**:

```bash
poedit -l ab,de,fg <<EOT
<msgid>	<ab>	<de>	<fg>
<msgid>	<ab>	<de>	<fg>
EOT
```

  Tabs separate fields. Do not feed poedit msgid copies or placeholders.
- **If any helper is slow, stop** — hand-translate (or pause and resume). Never
  block the task waiting on MT for gettext.

## README / man (AsciiDoc) — MT allowed with proxy

- Whole-document locale files under `man/<locale>/`. Prefer hand translation.
- For **long adoc/README only**, `googletranslator` may help — set the local
  HTTP proxy (`http://localhost:8118`; see **proxy.mdc**).
- That permission does **not** extend to gettext: if you are editing `.po`,
  go back to the section above and hand-translate.
- If `googletranslator` is too slow on adoc/README, **stop waiting and
  hand-translate** instead of leaving the job hung on MT.
